    {
      "id": "gt3fgh9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Right to Constitutional Remedies (Articles 32–35)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qmp6j6g"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Dr. B.R. Ambedkar called Article 32 the 'very heart and soul of the Indian Constitution'.",
        "Rights under Articles 20 and 21 cannot be suspended even during a National Emergency.",
        "Right to Property was deleted from Fundamental Rights by the 44th Amendment Act, 1978, and made a legal right under Article 300A.",
        "Article 17 (Abolition of Untouchability) is absolute and carries no reasonable restrictions."
      ],
      "id": "2nkltp0"
    },
